## Local Development

### Setup

```bash
# Start local PostgreSQL (Docker recommended)
docker run --name mercflow-db \
  -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=mercflow \
  -e POSTGRES_DB=mercflow_dev \
  -p 5432:5432 \
  -d postgres:16

# Run all pending migrations
npx medusa db:migrate

# Seed development data (if seed script exists)
npx medusa exec ./src/scripts/seed.ts
```

### Useful commands

```bash
npx medusa db:generate <module>   # Generate migration for a module
npx medusa db:migrate             # Run all pending migrations
npx medusa db:revert              # Revert the last migration batch
```

### Local vs. production

In local development, the agent runs migrations freely and iterates on schema as needed. In production or staging, no migration runs without explicit written instruction. See `conventions.mdc` for the full environment rules.
